{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527418-how-do-you-make-it-a-scary-christmas-for-the-pcs","id":1527418,"title":"How do you make it a Scary Christmas for the PCs?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-25T04:56:03-08:00","id":1527418,"title":"How do you make it a Scary Christmas for the PCs?","content":"Christmas is a major holiday with rich multilayered mythological and ritual implications. It's simply time for something to happen. So, in your version of the WoD how do you make it a Scary Christmas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T06:26:16-08:00","id":1527421,"title":"","content":"Several ways<br /> The most obvious one is the <b>Krampus</b><br /> While Santa rewarding the well-behaved children with gifst, the badly behaved ones only receive punishment from Krampus with birch rods... mind you birch branches are replaced with a whip in some representations<br /> Sometimes Krampus appears with a sack or a basket strapped to his back; this is to cart off evil children for drowning, eating, or transport to Hell.<br /> Some of the older versions make mention of naughty children being put in the bag and taken away...<br /> The Krampus is considered to be a half-goat, half-demon monster in some legends.<br /> Ultimately its role is to punish bad children or scare them into being good<br /> Be the (questionable) force of Good to teach the bad kids (and Child, you are a kid. Cub? You too.... you are a Changeling? Son, this bad boy a living nightmare... ) a lesson or a bona fide Demon summoned by a Baali (or a demonolgist, or anyone, really) he could be a scary force out of nightmares to begin with<br /> He could fly solo, or be with in gang with Santa's other companions, like <b>Belsnickel, Zwarte Piet</b> or even <b>Snegurochka</b><br /> <br /> \u200bThe other?<br /> <b>Santa himself</b><br /> In Changeling, the Dreaming. Santa is a Chimera, a creature made from dreams, and stories, and hopes. So Santa, world known and beloved by so many, is an incredibly powerful chimera, probably one who can manifest even in the real-world. It's canon that Santa comes to freehold and lives chimerical presents for childlings everywhere.<br /> Of course he is good as a Mage too (fun fact, in Marvel, Dr. Doom once mused if Santa Clause is a Sorcerer Supreme) - Santa after all technically changed the consensus of jesus's birthday and altered reality a big time so he is paradox free for one day<br /> <br /> But the most scary things could be the fact, Santa is none other tha <b>Odin, the All-father!</b><br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b\u200bSanta Clause flies around in December for Christmas to bring gifts to good children<br /> Odin flew around in December for Yuletide to head off the Wild Hunt. He knew who had been bad and good and hunted down or abducted those who deserved it.<br /> \u200b\u200bSanta have eight reindeer pulling his sleigh.<br /> Odin had an eight-legged horse, Sleipnir, that pulled his sleigh.<br /> Santa was depicted thin as often as chubby, and usually donned brown, blue, or red robes.<br /> Odin often depicted wearing either blue or brown robes.<br /> Santa have an army of elves who make toys for children.<br /> Elves and dwarves originate from Norse Mythology and are known as amazing creators.<br /> Santa sometimes is referred to as Father Christmas.<br /> Odin was referred to as Yule Father.<br /> <br /> Christmas has borrowed from Norse tradition include tree decoration, mistletoe, and wreaths.<br /> <br /> Now immagine Odin, either a a God, powerful spirit or just for fun a 4th Generation Gangrel Methuselah on chirstmas day blows his horn to start a Wild Hunt, and on his eight legged horse leads an army (wielding weapons forged in Nidavellir \u200bby Dwarves and/or Svartalfheim by Dark Elves) against whoever on his naughty list&quot; - be a Sept of Get o Fenrir, a rival Methuselah or just against Humanity itself...<br /> <br /> Yeah, it is<i> scarry</i><br /> <br /> He sees you when you're sleeping...<br /> He knows when you're awake...\u200b<br /> <br /> Have you been a good boy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T06:34:32-08:00","id":1527422,"title":"","content":"Didn\u2019t Jim Butcher do something with the Odin as Santa thing in the Dresden Files series?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 12-25-2023, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T19:31:32-08:00","id":1527447,"title":"","content":"Christmas happens around the winter solstice when night is longest. It's very easy to make that scary. There's a reason the English tell ghost stories at Christmas instead of Halloween.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-26T18:52:48-08:00","id":1527474,"title":"","content":"Candles and lit fireplaces everywhere, religious symbols prominently displayed all over, people going about in groups singing carols.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-26T19:24:06-08:00","id":1527476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527418-how-do-you-make-it-a-scary-christmas-for-the-pcs?p=1527474#post1527474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Candles and lit fireplaces everywhere, religious symbols prominently displayed all over, people going about in groups singing carols.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gruesome!!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T05:20:43-08:00","id":1528355,"title":"","content":"In the World of Darkness, Christmas takes on a haunting and ominous tone, weaving through a tapestry of supernatural elements that intensify the holiday's darker aspects. The air is thick with an unsettling energy as mysterious creatures and malevolent spirits exploit the festive season. The joyful carols become eerie chants, and the flickering lights cast sinister shadows. Beneath the veneer of gift-giving and celebration, a sense of foreboding permeates the night. The boundaries between the mundane and the supernatural blur, with creatures of the night emerging to exploit the heightened emotions of the season. Unsettling encounters with malevolent entities replace the warmth of traditional festivities, turning Christmas into a chilling and fear-inducing experience in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28323,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28323-leostehr","user":"LeoStehr","date":". 02-12-2024, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28323-leostehr","name":"LeoStehr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}